    "bytes": 200000,
    "meaning": "Bounded first-seen table/history for at most 4097 terms and a three-word result buffer."
  },
  "algorithm_details": {
    "map": "s(x) is the sum of positive proper divisors of x; s(1)=0. No value-zero divisor sum is needed because zero terminates the positive orbit.",
    "primary": "Store each in-cap positive value with its first sequence index; detect the first repeat to recover mu and lambda.",
    "independent_oracle": "Compute s(x) from prime factorization and linearly scan the prior-term list for the first repeat.",
    "cap_order": "At each in-cap value, classify zero/repetition first, then apply the transition cap, then compute its next aliquot value. An over-cap next value is reported immediately. A repeat or zero reached on the final permitted transition wins over the step-cap status.",
    "complexity": "At most 4096 transitions; each in-cap divisor-pair or factorization calculation is bounded by sqrt(100000). The sorted-table primary and linear-history reference are each O(T^2) worst case for T<=4097, with binary-search lookup in the primary."
  },
